AU  - Bozkurt, Ahmet Kursat; Balkanay, Ozan Onur; Dinc, Rasit
TI  - Catheter-guided endovenous cyanoacrylate closure is effective and safe in chronic venous insufficiency of the lower extremity: A Comparative Analysis
PY  - 2023
AB  - <title>Abstract</title><p><bold>Background</bold>Cyanoacrylate adhesive closure (CAC) systems have become widely used in the treatment of varicose veins. In terms of efficacy and safety, these non-thermal non-tumescent methods have been reported to be noninferior to endovenous thermal ablation techniques. There are no known published studies that compare products using CAC. VenaSeal® (Medtronic, Santa Rosa, Ca, USA) and VenaBlockⓇ (Invamed, Ankara, Turkey) are among the most commonly used CAC-based products worldwide. This review article focuses on the efficacy and safety of these two different commonly used products.<bold>Methods</bold>Published full-text research articles regarding the VenaBlock<sup>®</sup>System or the VenaSeal<sup>Ⓡ</sup>System was searched. Data for each product were evaluated by comparing them with each other in terms of effectiveness and safety.<bold>Results</bold>A total of 1882 extremities from 11 studies with VenaBlock<sup>®</sup>and 524 extremities from 8 studies with VenaSeal<sup>Ⓡ</sup>were included and compared. Both devices were observed to be effective and cumulative recanalization-free survival rates were similar (p = 0.188) at the 6th, 12th, 24th, 36th and 60th month follow-ups. Both products were found to improve VCSS and QoL scores.<bold>Conclusion</bold>Both devices were effective in terms of cumulative recanalization-free survival rates. Both significantly improved the venous clinical severity score and the quality of life scores. Cyanoacrylate adhesive closure is feasible in varicose vein treatment.</p>
