AU  - Almukhtar, Rawaa M; Goldman, Mitchel P
TI  - Large Varicose Vein Closure: A Comprehensive Review.
PY  - 2022
AB  - <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Treatment of chronic venous disease and varicose veins has significant psychosocial and economic impact. The great saphenous vein is a common vein to develop incompetence and reflux and, therefore, been the focus of therapy for many years.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE">To review the published medical literature relating to large varicose vein closure and provide a guide for closure techniques' efficacy and safety.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="METHODS">A comprehensive search of the English language literature was performed up to and including December 2021. All references pertaining to large varicose vein closure were reviewed.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS">There are multiple safe and effective minimally invasive methods to achieve occlusion of incompetent great saphenous vein, the most widely used of which is endovenous thermal ablation. Other nonthermal, tumescent, and nontumescent methods can also be used.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION">Proper knowledge of vein anatomy, ultrasound, and vein closure procedures is needed to ensure safe and effective outcomes.</AbstractText>
          <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2022 by the American Society for Dermatologic Surgery, Inc. Published by Wolters Kluwer Health, Inc. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
