AB  - <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Endovenous procedures are commonly used for varicose vein treatment.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Types, functionality, and significance of endovenous devices.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">To describe the different endovenous devices, their mode of action, inherent risks and efficacy according to the literature.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Long-term data confirm that endovenous procedures are equally effective as open surgery. Postoperative pain is minimal and downtime shorter after catheter interventions.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Catheter-based endovenous procedures increase the diversity of varicose vein treatment options. They are preferred by patients due to less pain and shorter downtime.</AbstractText>
